  "title": "South Korea’s Education Minister Resigns Over AI-Chased Exam Scandal",
  "summary": "A South Korean education minister resigned after an AI-assisted cheating scandal erupted during key university entrance exams, with fears of exam fraud rising following the top scorer admitting to using AI to cheat in a national tax exam. The resignation comes amid growing concerns about the effectiveness of existing anti-cheating measures.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Choi Kyo-jin admitted using AI to cheat in a national tax accountancy exam, leading to concerns about AI-assisted fraud in exams.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The education minister resigned after the scandal, signaling a shift in government response to the issue.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Public backlash and fears of exam fraud have led to new measures like loud phone alerts and eyeglass inspections.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
