      "title": "South Korean minister quits after AI cheating scandal engulfs university exams",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/22/south-korea-education-minister-resigns-after-ai-cheating-scandal-engulfs-university-exams",
      "description": "<p>Choi Kyo-jin says he ‘failed to prepare adequately’ for entrance exams following last-minute scramble to tighten measures</p><p>South Korea’s education minister has resigned after an AI-assisted cheating scandal that erupted in the lead-up to key university entrance exams last week.</p><p>The country has been gripped by fears of AI-assisted exam cheating since last Sunday, when the top scorer in a national tax accountancy exam <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/15/ai-cheating-south-korea-college-entrance-exam\">confessed to using a miniature camera and smartphone</a> to achieve a near-perfect score, just four days before the crucial university entrance exam, known as the <em>suneung</em>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/22/south-korea-education-minister-resigns-after-ai-cheating-scandal-engulfs-university-exams\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-22T12:12:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "South Korea’s Education Minister Resigns Over Anti-A.I. Cheating Rules",
